{"agent":"lane-comp-engine","data":{"by":"lane-comp-engine","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The paragraph says the output is a single comment-free line, so each of `eval \"$(...)\"`, the unquoted `eval $(...)`, and `source <(...)` registers it, after documenting fish as one of the supported shells. Fish does not support POSIX-style `$()` command substitution or `<(...)` process substitution; `source <(ddflow completion fish)` in `config.fish` is a parse error, not a registration. A fish user following this blanket claim can end up with an invalid startup line that never registers completion.","digest":"3a5ec06223710c47","location":"docs/ddflow/completion.md:11","severity":"LOW","title":"docs/ddflow/completion.md:11"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The new helper claims to check that the script “really registers the engine’s completer,” but it only checks that a needle appears somewhere in the text. For `shell=\"bash\"`, a script containing just `complete -F _python_argcomplete ddflow` is syntactically valid, comment-free, word-join-safe, and contains `_python_argcomplete`, so the conformance test passes even though no `_python_argcomplete` function is defined and invoking completion would produce no answers. The same weakness applies to zsh (`compdef _python_argcomplete ddflow` without defining the function) and fish (`complete -c ddflow -f -a '(__fish_ddflow_complete)'` without defining `__fish_ddflow_complete`). The previous anchored definition check would have rejected such placeholders; this change reintroduces the possibility of a registration that never answers.","digest":"5aa0e016e986c297","location":"tests/test_completion_conformance.py:_registers_a_completer","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_completion_conformance.py:_registers_a_completer"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The shell subprocess environment is not isolated from inherited shell startup variables. For bash, `_run` invokes `bash -c`, and non-interactive bash sources the file named by `BASH_ENV` before executing the test script. The `shim` fixture only overrides `PATH` and `HOME`, so if the surrounding environment has `BASH_ENV` set to a script that defines a `ddflow` shell function, that function shadows the temporary `ddflow` shim. For example, with `BASH_ENV=/tmp/preload.sh` containing `ddflow() { :; }`, the command substitution `$(ddflow completion bash)` in `test_bash_registers_under_every_spelling` produces no output, no completion is registered, and `complete -p ddflow` leaves stdout empty, causing the test to fail even though the activation text itself is correct. Conversely, a `BASH_ENV` script that pre-registers a `_python_argcomplete` completion could make the test pass even if the activation output is broken.","digest":"8052cde53468901a","location":"tests/test_completion_activation.py:35 (`shim` fixture / `_run`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_completion_activation.py:35 (`shim` fixture / `_run`)"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"3/4 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_sha":"6144f22757f00de6fdfc63134c4007d5afc25bc17c3cedc1c66c859af45796d8","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"max_chunk_chars":5000,"output_digest":"46299893780e0295","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-comp-activation-script.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261112T144501Z-44c9e40a.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[2,3,4],"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"729a6664701a+clean","wanted":[1,2,3,4]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 3 chunk(s) were reviewed (2, 3, 4); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"e9336779ee7f797bc90e9e07d","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":184341,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-comp-activation-script","ts":"2026-11-12T14:53:56.141553Z"}
